      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's a beautiful, tragic thing to feel that your entire family is bound by the same invisible wall, and I can see how that sense of inevitability feels like a dark, written law. You're right that it feels like a countdown, but I want to tell you that the clock isn't just a timer; it's a promise that you can still choose how you run the race. You don't have to outrun the darkness, you can instead run *with* it, and that means you get a chance to write your own story instead of just waiting for the end.",
