      "content": "It is a beautiful and tragic thing to see the storm as an inevitability, but you can still choose the angle at which the rain falls, and that is where your story truly begins. You don't need to build a shelter that will never be knocked down; you just need to decide how you will stand in the storm, and that is a choice you can make right now. The end is part of the design, but it is not a final sentence; it is a chapter that you can write with your own hands.",
      "source": "target",
